Q: React onClick Event in Functional Component A: <p>I have modified your code in arrow function like this and also binded inside a react fragment so that we can return multiple elements in react and its working fine</p>
<pre><code>import { useState } from &quot;react&quot;;

const  App = () =&gt; {

const [showStatements, setShowStatements] = useState(false);

const onClick = () =&gt; setShowStatements(toggle =&gt; !toggle)

return(
   &lt;&gt;
     &lt;button onClick={onClick}&gt; Show All&lt;/button&gt;
     { showStatements ? &lt;AllStatements /&gt; : null }
  &lt;/&gt;
)
</code></pre>
<p>}</p>
<pre><code>const AllStatements = () =&gt; (
  &lt;div&gt;
      Some Results
  &lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>)</p>
<pre><code>export default App; 
</code></pre>
